SUMMARY:Guided Meadow Exploration at Greenfield
DESCRIPTION:Exploring Greenfield’s Restored Meadows: A Guided Nature Walk\n \nMeadows are among the most vibrant and diverse ecosystems\, alive with color and activity. Join us for a guided hike with the Lancaster Conservancy through Greenfield’s restored meadows and experience the beauty and abundance of life they support. From native wildflowers to pollinators like butterflies and bees\, these habitats showcase the incredible connections within nature.\n\nThis slow-paced walk is perfect for anyone who enjoys observing the details of the natural world. Along the way\, we’ll discuss the restoration process\, the species that thrive here\, and why meadows are essential for biodiversity.\n\nEvent Highlights:\n\n– A leisurely hike through Greenfield’s restored meadows\n– Opportunities to see native flowers and pollinators up close\n– Insights into meadow ecology and restoration efforts\n \n\nDetails:\n\n– Easy\, slow-paced hike\n– Dress for the weather and bring drinking water\n– Suitable for ages 5 and up\n– Children must be accompanied by an adult\n– Participant capacity: 25\n \n\nThis event is free and open to all. RSVP preferred. \n            \n        \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/guided-meadow-exploration-at-greenfield-2/
LOCATION:Greenfield Lancaster\, 521 Greenfield Rd\, Lancaster\, 17601
CATEGORIES:Community
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/01/PhotOle_0040-scaled.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Greenfield":MAILTO:greenfieldinfo@high.net
END:VEVENT
